  "notes": "Unreal holds the _Opt cut (SM_53KSectorPit_Opt.fbx, 18,392 triangles); the pit is not re-exported, only the socket is new. The anchor is the existing crew entrance in the middle of the rear wall (outer row open to |y| < 80, inner row to |y| < 55, turned cheek bags at each row end); the neck walls (log face at +-82.5) close against the outer cheeks and the rear wall face (x -433, cheeks to -446). The neck brings the floor (mud + corduroy poles) through the entrance to 6 cm inside the pit's inner face (neck x -151), since the pit has no floor. Neck materials: SovTrench_Wood (slot 0), RL_Sandbag (slot 1, MI_Rus_SandBag_01 like the pit). Hidden triangles culled like the kit, with the pit as an extra occluder. Import the neck like the Soviet kit pieces, complex collision, no Nanite. Frame check: the _Opt FBX matches Unreal in triangle count and in y (mirrored) and x-min to 2 cm; the bounds quoted from Unreal (x max 282.5, z -14.1..81.3) are about 10 cm wider than the vertices (272.0, -3.7..71.9), which looks like bounds padding, not a different mesh or frame (the Rus53K doc gives the wall as x -4.46 to +2.73 m)."
